Print the shell code that integrates tmux-project into the shell. Add to
~/.bashrc:

  eval "$(tmux-project shell)"

or to ~/.zshrc:

  eval "$(tmux-project shell zsh)"

(don't forget the quotes)

Inside a tmux session the code sets SESSIONNAME and a per-session HISTFILE,
sources ~/.tmux.d/<session>.env and defines the pcd function.
